are listed per section.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Verdict (lead with impact)\n\n`Grok Bot` is **Anysphere's \"Cursor\" desktop-agent codebase, re-branded (\"sand\" codename) and pointed at x.ai's Grok models** — a cloud+local autonomous bot platform: bots that run on cloud boxes (\"Grok Bot's Computer\") or the local machine, driven by tools (shell/file/MCP/computer-use), with Slack/Teams/iMessage/SCM channels, bot templates shared via `grokbot://` deep links, voice calls over `wss://api.x.ai/`, and a Rust FIDO2 signing daemon for passkey delegation. The Cursor lineage leaks everywhere: bundle id `com.anysphere.sand`, `@anysphere/*` workspace deps, `cursor.com` homepage, `cursor-access-token`/`cursor-refresh-token` secret keys, `cursor://anysphere.cursor-mcp/oauth/return` MCP OAuth redirect, `review.cursor.com`, and the Cursor `checksum` request-signing algorithm — all inside a package whose author is \"SpaceXAI\".\n\n**Why this matters:** the app is a full agent-harness product (not a thin Grok chat client): 5,594 protobuf messages, 6 RPC services with 1,263 methods, a 40-tool local exec daemon, a 98-method coordinator, 111 structured `SAND-E*` error codes, and a 2,248-string i18n catalog. Everything a clean-room reimplementation needs is in the five sections below.\n\n## 2. Package & provenance\n\n| Layer | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Signed by | Developer ID Application: **Anysphere Incorporated (DCNK4UB866)**, notarized, Hardened Runtime (flags `0x10000`), entitlements: camera, audio-input, \n\n[... 9393 more characters truncated]\n\n[Assistant thinking]: Excellent — Phase 1-3 already done (prior analysis of the same 0.44.0 DMG exists). The user now says: \"start rebuild source code\" using the reference from refrence/ (which is the 0.18 reconstructed project). So the task is Phase 4: scaffold & reconstruction, using the 0.18 reconstructed repo as a template/reference.\n\nLet me look at the reference project structure to understand what \"rebuild source code\" means here — like