reconstruction, tests, manifests,\nbuild scripts, and Git LFS preservation copies of the original macOS arm64 and\nWindows x64 installers. It deliberately does **not** commit the extracted\nupstream application, build output, local credentials, or the large forensic\nrecovery workspace.\n\nThe public Grok Bot 0.18.0 application is instead treated as a pinned build\ninput. During bootstrap, the toolchain downloads it, verifies its SHA-256\nidentity, and extracts the pieces required to assemble the reconstruction.\n\nThe resulting app is a hybrid by design:\n\n- application runtimes are compiled from the readable sources under `source/`;\n- the polished shipped renderer remains the UI baseline;\n- a narrow deterministic transform adds the reconstructed Router settings U\n\n[... 2140 more characters truncated]\n\n[User]: use subagents for scoutings\n\n[Assistant thinking]: The user wants me to use subagents for scouting. Let me check the subagent tool guidance — need to call {action:\"list\",capabilities:true} first, then dispatch scout agents. Per safety guidance: first call list capabilities, then orchestrate. The task: scout the reference project structure and the extracted 0.44.0 analysis to plan the source rebuild.\n\nLet me load pi-subagents skill? The guidance says multi-step/parallel work: exactly one top-level subagent workflow call with async:true; children launch only inside it. And first call {action:\"list\",capabilities:true}.\n\nLet me do that first.\n\n[Assistant tool calls]: subagent(action=\"list\", capabilities=true)\n\n[Tool result]: Executable agents (capabilities):\nUser agents\n- gitnexus-cli (user): Description: Use when the user needs to run GitNexus CLI commands like analyze/index a repo, check status, clean the index, generate a wiki, or list indexed repos. Examples: \\\"Index this repo\\\", \\\"Reanalyze the codebase\\\", \\\"Generate a wiki\\\"; Tools: default/ambient; Model: zai/glm-5.3-flash; Thinking: high\n- gitnexus-debugging (user): D